.TH PEKA 1 "August 2026" "PEKA" "PEKA Commands"
.SH NAME
peka \- manage the PEKA application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peka app
.RI < start | stop | restart | status | logs >
.br
.B peka admin reset-password
.I username
.br
.B peka install
.br
.B peka doctor
.br
.B peka help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B peka
.RI [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peka
is the official command-line interface for a PEKA SaaS checkout. It manages
the native backend and frontend processes, bootstraps repository-owned
dependencies, performs non-destructive health checks, and provides controlled
Platform Admin recovery operations.
.PP
The command discovers the repository relative to its real executable path, so
it remains relocatable and works when invoked through a symbolic link.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B app
Manage the PEKA backend and frontend.
.TP
.B admin
Run Platform administration operations.
.TP
.B install
Prepare a fresh checkout.
.TP
.B doctor
Validate installation and runtime prerequisites.
.TP
.B help
Show top-level or command-specific help.
.SH APP COMMANDS
.TP
.B peka app start
Start the backend and frontend as background processes. PID files and logs are
stored under
.IR .runtime/ .
.TP
.B peka app stop
Stop processes owned by the recorded PID files. Already stopped processes are
handled successfully.
.TP
.B peka app restart
Stop and then start the application.
.TP
.B peka app status
Show backend and frontend state and their log paths.
.TP
.B peka app logs
Follow both application logs. Interrupt with Control-C.
.SH ADMIN COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "peka admin reset-password " username
Resolve an existing Platform Admin by exact username and generate the normal
24-hour, one-time PEKA reset URL. The command uses the application password-reset
service; it never accepts or writes a plaintext password.
.SH INSTALL
.B peka install
requires Python 3.11 or newer. It creates
.IR backend/.venv ,
upgrades pip, installs
.IR backend/requirements.txt ,
selects the frontend package manager from its lockfile, installs frontend
dependencies, creates runtime directories, and validates
.IR backend/.env .
.PP
The command prints the Alembic migration command required before application
startup. It does not assume an activated virtual environment.
.SH DOCTOR
.B peka doctor
checks the repository, Python, the backend virtual environment and imports,
frontend runtime and dependencies, configuration, database connectivity, and
whether the Alembic schema is at its heads. Checks are non-destructive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V , " " \-\-version
Show the version from the repository
.I VERSION
file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I VERSION
Shared PEKA application and CLI release version.
.TP
.I backend/.venv
Repository-owned Python virtual environment generated by
.BR "peka install" .
.TP
.I backend/.env
Backend configuration. It is not committed.
.TP
.I .runtime/pids
Application PID files.
.TP
.I .runtime/logs
Application logs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General command or health-check failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage.
.TP
.B 3
Missing dependency or incomplete installation.
.TP
.B 4
Administrative operation rejected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
./cli/peka install
./cli/peka doctor
./cli/peka app start
./cli/peka app status
./cli/peka admin reset-password kenady
man ./docs/man/peka.1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1),
.BR npm (1),
.BR alembic (1),
.BR uvicorn (1)
